    VALUES (NULL, $q$Forging - Mechanical press$q$, 'process', 'single', false, true, true, $q$Forging on a mechanical press with a transfer between its stations: every stroke finishes one forging, so the time per forging is one stroke at the press's stroke rate. The rate is the press's highest; the reference data's stroke rate by part complexity is not used, because it does not say how the complexity score of a part is found.$q$)
